  "intro": {
    "language": "en",
    "text": "Alèxia Putellas i Segura (born 4 February 1994), often known simply as Alexia, is a Spanish professional footballer from Catalonia who plays as a midfielder or forward for the Women's Super League club London City Lionesses and the Spain women's national team. She previously played for the clubs Espanyol, Levante, and Barcelona, and has also played for the Catalonia women's national team. She has won all the major club awards and most of the individual awards available to a European player, and is widely regarded as one of the greatest female footballers of all time.\nPutellas started her youth career at CE Sabadell, passing through Barcelona before she moved to Espanyol, where she played most of her youth football. After a year at Levante she returned to Barcelona in 2012, where she won eight league titles, eight Copas de la Reina, four Supercopa de España Femenina (Spanish Women's Super Cup) and four UEFA Women's Champions League trophies. In Barcelona's 2020–21 season, she played an essential role as her team won the Champions League as well as the resulting continental treble, both for the first time in their history. Putellas then went on to win the UEFA Women's Player of the Year...",
    "sourceId": "wikipedia-en",
    "usage": "Research excerpt; paraphrase and cross-check before publication."
  },
